  <prompt>Create the reusable docked side-pane framework in @spaarke/ui-components: SprkSidePaneHost (wraps SidePaneShell for chrome, generalizes DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator's lifecycle for createPane / mutual-exclusion / close-on-navigate / unload cleanup) plus a static sidePaneRegistry ({ id, icon, title, order, component }) that drives right-rail icons. One registry entry = one rail icon = one contributor. Host and registry live in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Fluent UI v9 + React shared-component and Xrm.App.sidePanes lifecycle expertise. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>New SprkSidePaneHost component + sidePaneRegistry module + right-rail icon rendering under src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/, wired to the widened xrmContext typings (010), with unit + render tests. The host renders the active contributor selected from the registry; adding/removing a registry entry adds/removes exactly one rail icon.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Per spec FR-01 + plan.md Phase 1 task 011 (and OQ-9 resolved: SidePaneShell is presentational-only → wrap, don't extend). The host generalizes the de-facto pane host DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator (idempotent createPane, mutuallyExclusiveWith, attachVisibilityLifecycle IntersectionObserver close-on-navigate, unload cleanup) into an app-wide, multi-contributor seam so future spaarke-side-pane-* features register rather than re-implement pane plumbing. Registry ergonomics follow WorkspaceWidgetRegistry + surfaceLaunchRegistry.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/SprkSidePaneHost.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/sidePaneRegistry.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/__tests__/SprkSidePaneHost.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/SidePaneShell.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/sidePane/DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/registry/WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/surfaceHandoff/surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/xrmContext.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Widened xrmContext typings (getPane/pane.select, webresourceName, 3-frame getXrm) the host uses for createPane/select/frame-walk.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Wrap SidePaneShell for chrome (presentational-only); generalize DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator lifecycle — do NOT reinvent createPane / close-on-navigate / unload cleanup (NFR-08 reuse, OQ-9 resolved).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The pane MUST be created via Xrm.App.sidePanes.createPane with canClose:false + alwaysRender:true (spec MUST rule / NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 tokens only; portal FluentProvider re-wrap for any portalled surface; honor light/dark via code-page theme detection and --sprk-ui-scale via scaledTheme/useUiScale (NFR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">@spaarke/ui-components code MUST stay React-16/17-safe: no createRoot; use JSXElement not JSX.Element.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Host-context only — no BFF, no plugin, no per-form web resource.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <topic>Fluent v9 shared side-pane host + static contributor registry + Xrm.App.sidePanes lifecycle</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-portal-gotcha.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Generalize the orchestrator" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/sidePane/DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator.ts">Lift idempotent createPane, mutuallyExclusiveWith, attachVisibilityLifecycle (IntersectionObserver close-on-navigate), and unload cleanup into the pane-agnostic SprkSidePaneHost lifecycle.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Wrap the shell" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/SidePaneShell.tsx">Compose SidePaneShell for chrome; do not add host logic to it.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Static code-owned registry" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/surfaceHandoff/surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts">Model sidePaneRegistry as a code-owned static table ({ id, icon, title, order, component }); WorkspaceWidgetRegistry adds the Map + lazy-factory + metadata ergonomics.</pattern>
      <pattern name="--sprk-ui-scale" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/scaledTheme.ts">Apply the scaled Fluent theme + useUiScale wiring for NFR-07.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor (FULL) + model-tier (sonnet) + effort (high) per task-execute Step 0.5; load the knowledge files and read the four canonical-reference files.</step>
    <step order="1">Define sidePaneRegistry.ts: a code-owned static table entry shape { id, icon, title, order, component } (component lazy-loadable), with register/get/list helpers modeled on surfaceLaunchRegistry + WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.</step>
    <step order="2">Generalize DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator's lifecycle (idempotent createPane with canClose:false + alwaysRender:true, mutuallyExclusiveWith, attachVisibilityLifecycle close-on-navigate, unload cleanup) into a pane-agnostic core used by SprkSidePaneHost — via the widened xrmContext getPane/pane.select/getXrm.</step>
    <step order="3">Build SprkSidePaneHost.tsx: wrap SidePaneShell for chrome; render right-rail icons from the registry (sorted by order); render the active contributor's component; theme via scaledTheme/useUiScale + portal FluentProvider re-wrap (ADR-021).</step>
    <step order="4">Handle the unknown-id case: selecting/looking up a registry id that is not registered degrades gracefully (renders nothing / a benign empty state; never throws).</step>
    <step order="5">Author tests in __tests__/SprkSidePaneHost.test.tsx: host renders the active contributor from the registry; registry add/remove maps to exactly one rail-icon add/remove; render in light AND dark; portal re-wrap present (ADR-021); unknown id does not throw.</step>
    <step order="6">Recompile @spaarke/ui-components and run unit + render tests; confirm green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set task 011 status to completed.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator cannot be generalized without breaking its existing DataGrid consumers, STOP and escalate (root §6.5 — reuse-vs-fork decision): propose either a shared extracted core both consume, or a documented project-scoped fork, rather than silently duplicating pane plumbing.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>SidePaneShell.tsx (presentational chrome only, OQ-9 confirmed); DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator.ts (de-facto pane host: createPane + mutuallyExclusiveWith + attachVisibilityLifecycle close-on-navigate + unload cleanup); WorkspaceWidgetRegistry.ts + surfaceLaunchRegistry.ts (registry precedents).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the parts that exist — wrap SidePaneShell, generalize DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator, follow the registry precedents. No for the genuinely new part: an app-wide, multi-contributor registry seam that binds contributors to right-rail icons for the whole MDA shell (neither the shell nor the DataGrid-scoped orchestrator provides this).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the shared host + registry, every future quick-access feature re-implements createPane / close-on-navigate / unload plumbing → divergent, drifting panes (the retired SidePaneManager is the cautionary example), and Navigator (the first tenant) has no host to register against.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Host renders active contributor in light and dark">
      <steps>
        <step>Register one contributor in sidePaneRegistry and mount SprkSidePaneHost in light theme.</step>
        <step>Re-mount in dark theme (data-theme=dark / prefers-color-scheme dark).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The active contributor renders with Fluent v9 tokens honoring light and dark correctly (no hardcoded colors); layout unchanged across themes.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="One registry entry = one rail icon (ADR-021 portal check)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the host with N registry entries; count right-rail icons.</step>
        <step>Add one entry and remove one entry; re-count.</step>
        <step>Inspect any portalled surface for a FluentProvider re-wrap.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Rail icon count equals registry entry count; adding/removing an entry changes the count by exactly one; portalled content is wrapped in its own FluentProvider (ADR-021 portal gotcha).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Unknown registry id degrades gracefully">
      <steps>
        <step>Select/look up a registry id that is not registered.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The host renders a benign empty state and does not throw.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Recompile @spaarke/ui-components + run Jest unit/render tests.</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/SprkSidePaneHost.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/sidePaneRegistry.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/__tests__/SprkSidePaneHost.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a populated sidePaneRegistry, when SprkSidePaneHost renders, then it renders the active contributor's component selected from the registry.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the host is rendered, when a registry entry is added or removed, then exactly one right-rail icon is added or removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the host creates the app pane, when createPane is called, then it uses canClose:false + alwaysRender:true.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given light and dark themes, when the host renders, then Fluent v9 tokens honor both correctly with a portal FluentProvider re-wrap (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unknown registry id, when the host looks it up/selects it, then it degrades gracefully (no throw).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit + render tests pass; shared-lib build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Maps to spec FR-01 (+ FR-13 framework-proof, exercised later by stub task 085) and plan.md Phase 1 task 011. NFR-08 reuse is mandatory: wrap SidePaneShell, generalize DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator, follow WorkspaceWidgetRegistry/surfaceLaunchRegistry. Run /conflict-check before the @spaarke/ui-components PR (shared lib touched by other worktrees; SidePane/ subfolder currently untouched).

COMPLETED 2026-08-13 (sonnet, FULL rigor). Escalation trigger did NOT fire — DataGridSidePaneOrchestrator.ts was GENERALIZED IN PLACE (not forked): two additive fields (`webResourceName` made optional; new `alwaysRender` passthrough) plus a swap from the untyped `services/xrmGlobal.ts` getXrm() to the widened `utils/xrmContext.ts` getXrm() (task 010, same runtime semantics, adds typing). Zero behavior change for the sole existing consumer (EventsPage/src/App.tsx — always passes webResourceName, never sets alwaysRender). Built: sidePaneRegistry.ts (static contributor table, lazy factory + resolve/cache per WorkspaceWidgetRegistry, resolve->undefined-never-throw per surfaceLaunchRegistry), SprkSidePaneHost.tsx (wraps SidePaneShell + PaneHeader for chrome; right-rail icon strip; idempotent createPane via the generalized orchestrator with canClose:false+alwaysRender:true; theme via resolveCodePageTheme/setupCodePageThemeListener + useUiScale/scaleTheme + --sprk-ui-scale CSS var per the SpaarkeAi/LegalWorkspace app-shell precedent; explicit ADR-021 portal FluentProvider re-wrap on the rail Tooltip content), __tests__/SprkSidePaneHost.test.tsx (11 tests, all passing). Verification: `npm run build` (tsc) clean; `npx jest src/components/SidePane src/components/DataGrid` 75/75 green (DataGrid regression proves existing consumers unaffected); `npx eslint` clean on all new/modified files (one PRE-EXISTING unrelated warning left untouched in the orchestrator's catch block). Full suite (`npx jest`) has 10 pre-existing failing suites unrelated to this task (surfaceLaunchRegistry, ConversationView, XrmDataverseClient, etc. — none touch SidePane/DataGrid/xrmContext) — not introduced by task 011, left as-is per scope boundary.</notes>
